---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/afterframe-b.css';

/* Arm "b" of the /afterframe test (see src/lib/afterframe.ts). Converted
   from the standalone concept listings-3-grid.html; the direction contract is the first
   comment inside the page root (Astro strips a slot's leading comment; a
   deeper one survives). */
---
<Base title="Afterframe · Tonight's listings" description="A new kind of film companion for Plex. Tonight's schedule, and the moments you kept, at the minute you kept them. The film never stops." fonts={['family=League+Gothic', 'family=Barlow:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;1,400', 'family=Silkscreen:wght@400;700']}>

<div class="af-root">
<!--
DIRECTION CONTRACT · seed 8534e8c8 · mode persuade
THESIS: (third cut: a kept frame is followed by its sent event in the column, the sharing block leads with the conversation, the header runner rewrites Keep to Share in teletext while it is on screen) The listings grid is the whole page. Time runs down the left edge from 22:00 to closedown, every section is a programme block at the hour it happens, and the moments you kept sit in their own column at the minute you kept them. Refuses sections; there is only the schedule.
OWN-WORLD: teletext black, yellow for now, cyan for next, grey for later, orange only for the kept frame; Silkscreen at integer scale; League Gothic block titles; Barlow body; a NOW line across the grid that moves with the clock; fastext keys, a keypad, a CRT switch.
STORY: visitor reads P100 at 22:00, sees Furious on now with a frame kept at 22:39 beside it, scrolls down the evening through how it works, the library, sharing and the index, and reaches closedown and the red key.
FIRST VIEWPORT: header with keypad and clock; the P100 row; the schedule begins: the 22:00 cell, a black block with the headline, lede and keys spanning programme and kept columns; the 22:15 row starts Furious in yellow with the kept frame at 22:39 in the right column and the NOW line crossing at 22:47.
FORM: television listings, the grid-as-page variant of option E. Raise: sequence carried only by time, which is real on every row.
FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
-->
<header class="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="#main" aria-label="Afterframe home"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/shots/afterframe/icon.png" alt="" width="26" height="26"><span>Afterframe</span></a>
    <div class="clock"><form class="keypad" id="keypad" aria-label="Type a page number"><span class="tx w">P</span><input class="tx w" id="pin" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" maxlength="3" value="100" aria-label="Page number"></form><span class="tx d date">Sat 19 Sep</span><span class="tx y" id="clock">22:47:12</span><button type="button" class="crt-sw tx d" id="crtsw" aria-pressed="false">CRT</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="runner"><div class="wrap"><span class="tx" id="runner" aria-live="polite">KEEP WHAT STAYED WITH YOU</span><span class="tx d right" id="runner-right">Tonight · 22:00 → closedown</span></div></div>
</header>

<main id="main" class="wrap">
  <div class="pagehead"><span class="tx dh"><b>P100</b> Afterframe · Tonight</span><span class="tx d meta"><span>Plex</span><span>Apple TV</span><span>Living room</span><span>22:00 → closedown</span></span></div>
  <div class="mosaic" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="sched" id="sched">
    <div class="nowline" id="nowline" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <!-- 22:00 · P100 -->
    <div class="tcell h" data-t="22:00"><div class="in"><span class="tx">22:00</span><span class="lab">P100</span></div></div>
    <section class="af-hero blk" style="grid-row:1" data-page="100" data-time="22:00 · P100" aria-labelledby="h1">
      <h1 id="h1">Keep what stayed with&nbsp;you.</h1>
      <p class="lede measure">A new kind of film companion. Reach back to a moment playing from Plex, keep the frame and its words, and never interrupt the television. Tonight's schedule runs down the page. What you kept is in the right-hand column, at the minute you kept it.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="key" href="/afterframe/b/go/">Join the early list</a>
        <a class="key cyan" href="#p101">How it works · 23:10</a>
      </div>
      <div class="legend">
        <span class="tx"><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--tx-yellow)"></span> On now</span>
        <span class="tx"><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--tx-cyan)"></span> Next</span>
        <span class="tx"><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--later)"></span> Later</span>
        <span class="tx"><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--pin); border-radius:50%"></span> A moment you kept</span>
        <span class="tx"><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--tx-cyan); border-radius:50%"></span> Sent on</span>
        <span class="tx"><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--tx-red); width:2px"></span> Now · the television never stopped</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 22:15 · Furious -->
    <div class="tcell" data-t="22:15"><div class="in"><span class="tx">22:15</span><span class="lab">Apple TV</span></div></div>
    <section class="blk now" style="grid-row:2 / span 4" data-time="22:15 · Apple TV" aria-labelledby="h-fur">
      <div class="head"><h2 id="h-fur">Furious · They Make a Noise Like Feathers</h2><span class="tx d meta"><span>S01E06</span><span>22:15 – 23:10</span><span>54:45</span><span>on now</span></span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <div>
          <h3>Save the scene without stopping it.</h3>
          <p>Afterframe is a companion, not a remote. It reads the active session and retrieves the selected moment from your own Plex server. It never pauses, seeks, or commands playback on Apple TV. At 22:39 a frame was kept from this episode. The programme did not notice.</p>
          <p>Some moments arrive before you are ready for them. A composition. A glance. A line that changes the scene. Open the Companion and move through the last two minutes until you find the frame that caught you. No scramble for the remote. No photographing the screen. No asking everyone to wait.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="phone-row"><figure><div class="phone"><video poster="/shots/afterframe/now.webp" muted loop playsinline autoplay preload="metadata" aria-label="Afterframe's Now screen while Furious plays: the timeline advances, the plate is pressed, the frame drops into Tonight and the clock keeps counting"><source src="/shots/afterframe/loop/keep.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video></div><figcaption class="tx d">Now · 22:39 · the film never stops</figcaption></figure></div>
      </div>
