    <div class="tcell" data-t="00:45"><div class="in"><span class="tx">00:45</span></div></div>

    <!-- 01:02 · In the Mood for Love · P103 P104 -->
    <div class="tcell h" data-t="01:00"><div class="in"><span class="tx">01:00</span><span class="lab">P103 · P104</span></div></div>
    <section class="blk later" id="p103" style="grid-row:13 / span 7" data-page="103" data-time="01:02 · Apple TV · P103" aria-labelledby="h-itmfl">
      <div class="head"><h2 id="h-itmfl">In the Mood for Love</h2><span class="tx d meta"><span>2000</span><span>01:02 – 02:41</span><span>01:38:40</span><span>later</span></span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <div>
          <h3>The frame goes where you were already talking.</h3>
          <p>Some moments immediately make you think of someone. The share sheet is the iPhone's own, so the frame lands in the group chat, the thread, or the post, with its line or its timecode when they help. The private original and the reason you kept it stay in Afterframe. At 22:56 the Furious frame went to the group chat; two replies came back before the scene ended.</p>
          <div class="stills" style="margin-top:16px" aria-label="Sending a frame">
            <div class="still"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="920" height="497" src="/shots/afterframe/stills/sh-sheet.jpg" alt="The iPhone share sheet with the frame at the top" data-mosaic><span class="tx">22:56 · share sheet</span></div>
            <div class="still"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="840" height="454" src="/shots/afterframe/stills/sh-compose.jpg" alt="A new message with the frame and the words: I have no notes" data-mosaic><span class="tx">22:56 · into the thread</span></div>
          </div>
