    <!-- 02:41 · Closedown · P105 P199 -->
    <div class="tcell h" data-t="02:45"><div class="in"><span class="tx">02:45</span><span class="lab">P105 · P199</span></div></div>
    <section class="blk faq" id="p105" style="grid-row:20" data-page="105" data-time="02:41 · Closedown · P105" aria-labelledby="h-close">
      <div class="head"><h2 id="h-close">Closedown · Questions from the sofa</h2><span class="tx d meta"><span>P105</span><span>7 entries</span><span>1/1</span></span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <div>
          <details><summary>Does Afterframe take a screenshot of my Apple TV?</summary><p>No. Afterframe does not record or mirror the television. It retrieves a frame from your Plex Media Server near the selected playback position.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Will it pause or seek what I am watching?</summary><p>No. Afterframe observes playback and never pauses, seeks, stops, or otherwise controls your Apple TV.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Is capture frame-perfect?</summary><p>Afterframe uses the indexed frames available from Plex and captures the frame it shows you. It is designed around trustworthy moment selection rather than claiming arbitrary frame-by-frame precision.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Does it preserve subtitles?</summary><p>When Afterframe can resolve a supported text subtitle cue, it can keep that dialogue and create an optional subtitled rendition. Afterframe subtitles are rendered separately; they are not a reproduction of the subtitles on Apple TV.</p></details>
        </div>
        <div>
          <details><summary>Do I have to write a note?</summary><p>Never. A capture without a note is complete. Writing is there when a moment gives you something to say.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Is Afterframe a social network?</summary><p>No. There is no public feed or profile. Your library is private; sharing happens deliberately through the services and conversations you already use.</p></details>
          <details><summary>What do I need?</summary><p>The first release is designed for an iPhone running iOS 26 or later, access to a Plex Media Server, and a configured Apple TV Plex client. It does not capture from third-party streaming services.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="p199" data-page="199" style="margin-top:12px">
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 5rem); color:var(--tx-yellow)">Every film leaves something behind.</h2>
